  "baselineReason": "C23 is the newer published standard, but installed GCC14.2 documents C23 support as experimental/incomplete and reports202000 in its c23 mode. C17 gives a stable supported portable teaching baseline. N1570 primary committee draft supplies unchanged core clauses; GCC docs describe C17 defect-correction relationship. Do not claim complete C23 support.",
  "compilerPolicy": "Actual GCC14.2 -std=c17 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror; no intentional undefined-behavior execution. All examples must avoid implementation-specific numeric assumptions or explicitly disclose them. Optional C11 threads/atomics verified against actual runtime, not universally available claim.",
  "exclusions": [
    "Every standard-library API or C23-only addition",
    "OS-specific sockets/processes/POSIX APIs, embedded register programming and kernel internals",
    "Custom allocators, lock-free algorithms, complex signal handling, variadic implementations and ABI/FFI specialization",
    "Unsafe undefined-behavior demonstrations executed as if deterministic",
    "Graphics/game engines and production security certification"
  ],
